---
/**
 * The exercise catalog as tappable tiles; tapping appends a step
 * (`routineBuilder().addStep`). Reads `catalog`/`steps`/`maxSteps` from the
 * parent scope (`maxSteps` is `routineBuilder()`'s reactive mirror of
 * `MAX_BUILDER_STEPS`, not a frontmatter import — see the note below).
 * Hand-rolled per `components/CLAUDE.md`'s "multi-part custom control a
 * shared primitive cannot express as-is" exemption (precedent:
 * `AppModeForm.astro`): each tile needs its own dynamic name/description
 * text and a per-clone disabled state, and `Button.astro` offers neither a
 * default slot nor an Alpine-bindable label to carry either.
 *
 * Bounds always cross this boundary as directive-string reads of the
 * factory's own reactive state (`:disabled="... maxSteps"` below), never as
 * a frontmatter import of a value from `routine-builder.data.ts`: that
 * module is browser-only (`globalThis.location`, `fetch` via
 * `@client/api/*`), and an `.astro` frontmatter import would run it during
 * SSR/prerendering instead.
 */
---

<section class="space-y-2">
  <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-foreground">Add an exercise</h2>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
    <template
      x-for="entry in catalog"
      :key="entry.exerciseTemplateId"
    >
      <button
        type="button"
        class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-accent px-3 py-2.5 text-left transition-colors duration-150 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-40"
        :disabled="steps.length >= maxSteps"
        @click="addStep(entry)"
      >
        <span
          class="block text-sm font-semibold text-foreground"
          x-text="entry.name"
        ></span>
        <span
          class="block text-xs text-muted-foreground"
          x-text="entry.description ?? ''"
        ></span>
      </button>
    </template>
  </div>
</section>
